{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 10, 13]], "date-time": "2026-10-13T16:39:47Z", "timestamp": 1791909587664, "version": "4.3.4"}, "reference-count": 82, "publisher": "Wiley", "issue": "11", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2025, 1, 26]], "date-time": "2025-01-26T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1737849600000}, "content-version": "vor", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}], "funder": [{"DOI": "10.13039/501100001659", "name": "Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "award": ["390874152"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["390874152"]}], "id": [{"id": "10.13039/501100001659", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}]}, {"DOI": "10.13039/501100001659", "name": "Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "award": ["390776260"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["390776260"]}], "id": [{"id": "10.13039/501100001659", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}]}, {"DOI": "10.13039/100010661", "name": "Horizon 2020 Framework Programme", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "award": ["957213"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["957213"]}], "id": [{"id": "10.13039/100010661", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}]}], "content-domain": {"domain": ["advanced.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"], "crossmark-restriction": true}, "short-container-title": ["Advanced Energy Materials"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2025, 3]]}, "abstract": "<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>High\u2010performance batteries need accelerated discovery and optimization of new anode materials. Herein, we explore the Si\u2500Ge\u2500Sn ternary alloy system as a candidate fast\u2010charging anode materials system by utilizing a scanning droplet cell (SDC) as an autonomous electrochemical characterization tool with the goal of subsequent upscaling. As the SDC is performing experiments sequentially, an exploration of the entire ternary space is unfeasible due to time constraints. Thus, closed\u2010loop optimization, guided by real\u2010time data analysis and sequential learning algorithms, is utilized to direct experiments. The lead material identified is scaled up to a coin cell to validate the findings from the autonomous millimeter\u2010scale thin\u2010film electrochemical experimentation. Explainable machine learning (ML) models incorporating data from high\u2010throughput Raman spectroscopy and X\u2010ray diffraction (XRD) are used to elucidate the effect of short and long\u2010range ordering on material performance.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1002/aenm.202404961", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2025, 1, 27]], "date-time": "2025-01-27T02:12:51Z", "timestamp": 1737943971000}, "update-policy": "https://doi.org/10.1002/crossmark_policy", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 28, "title": ["Integrating Automated Electrochemistry and High\u2010Throughput Characterization with Machine Learning to Explore Si\u2500Ge\u2500Sn Thin\u2010Film Lithium Battery Anodes"], "prefix": "10.1002", "volume": "15", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1796-9224", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Alexey", "family": "Sanin", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "Helmholtz Institute Ulm (HIU)  Helmholtzstr. 11 89081 Ulm Germany"}, {"name": "Karlsruhe Institute of Technology (KIT)  76021 Karlsruhe Germany"}, {"name": "Technical University of Munich (TUM) TUM School of Natural Sciences Department of Chemistry Chair of Digital Catalysis  Lichtenbergstr. 4 85748 Garching Germany"}, {"name": "Technical University of Munich (TUM) Munich Data Science Institute (MDSI)  Walther\u2010von\u2010Dyck\u2010Str. 10 85748 Garching Germany"}, {"name": "Technical University of Munich (TUM) Munich Institute of Robotics and Machine Intelligence (MIRMI)  Georg\u2010Brauchle\u2010Ring 60 80992 Munich Germany"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Jackson K.", "family": "Flowers", "sequence": "additional",